WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.177
Tool calling and agentic behavior are related, but they are not the same thing.

00:00:05.177 --> 00:00:08.772
A single tool call can be one model decision.

00:00:08.772 --> 00:00:15.007
The user asks for weather, the model proposes the weather function, the application runs it,

00:00:15.007 --> 00:00:17.537
and the model produces an answer.

00:00:17.537 --> 00:00:20.167
An agent adds a control loop.

00:00:20.167 --> 00:00:27.222
It observes the current state, decides what to do, may call a tool, observes the result, updates its state,

00:00:27.222 --> 00:00:32.114
and decides again until a stopping condition is reached.

00:00:32.599 --> 00:00:35.156
Agentic does not mean uncontrolled.

00:00:35.156 --> 00:00:43.386
A useful agent still needs allowed actions, validation, permissions, state management, stopping conditions,

00:00:43.386 --> 00:00:45.846
and evaluation around the L L M.
